From: Adam Matthews <52178922+adamsthws@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tcg: take turns between vCPUs every millisecond, not every 100

One thread of QEMU runs an ESP32's two cores in turn, each until the next kick,
100 ms of virtual time by default. Firmware on one core reading flash spins
with its interrupts off until the other core has parked, which it does only
when its turn comes: up to 100 ms for each flash read, where a real chip takes
microseconds. So stock firmware spinning on a lock at start-up trips its
interrupt watchdog and resets, over and over. A single-core guest, an
ESP32-C3's, has no kick timer and is not affected.
---
diff --git a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.h b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.h
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.h
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.h
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 #ifndef TCG_ACCEL_OPS_RR_H
 #define TCG_ACCEL_OPS_RR_H

-#define TCG_KICK_PERIOD (NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND / 10)
+#define TCG_KICK_PERIOD (NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND / 1000)

 /* Kick all RR vCPUs. */
 void rr_kick_vcpu_thread(CPUState *unused);
